CREATED:20260915T201405Z
DESCRIPTION:Duke medical student Kiran Masroor\, selected as this year's C
 . Eric Lincoln Theology and Arts Fellow\, will give a talk on her exhibit
 ion "Sacred are the waters."\n\nFree admission.\n\nOn display in Duke Cha
 pel from October 2 through November 5\, "Sacred are the waters" presents 
 thirteen poems framed individually but all part of one mythological cosmo
 logy. They interweave themes of life and death\, building to a climactic 
 section that expresses that tension in ecstatic release.\n\nMasroor is di
 splaying her cycle of original poems as this year's recipient of the C. E
 ric Lincoln Theology and Arts Fellowship\, which provides funding for a D
 uke student to complete a sacred art project and display it in the Chapel
 . Her poetry has been published in VOICES Magazine\, Muzzle Magazine\, th
 e Yale Daily News\, and the anthology Without a Doubt: poems illuminating
  faith. Her poem "Interrupted Connection" received second place in the fo
 rty-fourth annual William Carlos William poetry competition. \n\nLearn mo
 re at https://chapel.duke.edu/news/exhibition-students-poems-probes-bound
 aries-life-and-death/
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260915T201405Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261019T173000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T201405Z
